Bubble Sort: 

    Description: It's comparing the adjecent elements and swapping them if they are in the wrong order.
    Time Complexity: O(n^2)
    Best Case: O(n)
    Worst Case: O(n^2)
    Space Complexity: O(1)
    Stable: Yes
    In-place: Yes

    def bubbleSort(arr):
        n = len(arr)
        for i in range(n):
            for j in range(0, n - i - 1): (Last part is sorted, n-i-1 points to last unsorted num)
                if arr[j] > arr[j + 1]:
                    arr[j], arr[j + 1] = arr[j + 1], arr[j]
        return arr

Selection Sort:

    Description: It's finding the minimum element and swapping it with the first element.
    Time Complexity: O(n^2)
        Best Case: O(n)
        Worst Case: O(n^2)
    Space Complexity: O(1)
    Stable: No
    In-place: Yes

    def selectionSort(arr):
        n = len(arr)
        for i in range(n):
            min_idx = i
            for j in range(i + 1, n):
                if arr[j] < arr[min_idx]:
                    min_idx = j
            arr[i], arr[min_idx] = arr[min_idx], arr[i]
        return arr

Insertion Sort:

    Description: It consists of 2 parts sorted array and unsorrted array, 
                 first part is sorted and second part is unsorted.
                 iterate through the unsorted part and insert the element at the right index in sorted part.
    Time Complexity: O(n^2)
        Best Case: O(n)
        Worst Case: O(n^2)
    Space Complexity: O(1)
    Stable: Yes
    In-place: Yes

    def insertionSort(arr):
        n = len(arr)
        for i in range(1, n):
            key = arr[i]
            j = i - 1
            while j >= 0 and key < arr[j]: (j>=0 is for j-=1)(other is for finding right place)
                arr[j + 1] = arr[j] (we shift the element to the right)
                j -= 1 (J moveds from right to left)
            arr[j + 1] = key
        return arr

